<title>GERMANY: E. German construction wages held steady till 1998.</title>
<headline>E. German construction wages held steady till 1998.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German construction employers' union said on Tuesday that wages for about 360,000 workers in east Germany will be held steady until May 1998 under terms of a deal reached with union IG Bau.</p>
<p>The agreement means that a plan to gradually increase wages to west German levels has been suspended.</p>
<p>The east German economy has suffered in its transformation to a market economy from rapid wage increases to bring eastern pay into line with western wages. The sharp wage gains have not been matched by gains in output and productivity.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
